# Cova — tinder for your home

# iOS AI-powered interior design app

# Bundle ID: ai.cova.app

## CRITICAL: BEFORE EVERY PROMPT

- Always read @BUILDGUIDE.md for the relevant phase and step before writing any code
- Always read @MASTER_STRATEGY.md for feature behavior and product decisions
- Every implementation decision must align with these two documents
- Do not deviate unless explicitly told to by Pranav or Daksh

## CRITICAL VERSION LOCKS — NEVER CHANGE

expo: ~52.0.49
react: 18.3.1 EXACT — no caret
react-dom: 18.3.1 EXACT — no caret
@react-three/fiber: 8.17.10 EXACT — no caret
@react-three/drei: 9.88.0 EXACT — no caret
three: 0.155.0 EXACT — no caret
node: 20.x (never 22+)

## Architecture

- Monorepo: pnpm workspaces. Root cova/, apps/mobile/, packages/shared/
- App: React Native + Expo SDK 52, iOS only for V1
- State: Zustand with immer middleware — never useState for global state
- Navigation: React Navigation 6 — bottom tabs + stack
- Backend: Supabase — all external calls go through Edge Functions
- Never put API keys in client code — only Supabase anon key and URL in .env
- Never use useEffect for data fetching — use Zustand store actions
- Always handle loading, error, and empty states in UI components
- TypeScript strict mode throughout — never use 'any'
- Import shared types from '@cova/shared'

## 3D Rules

- NEVER use OrbitControls — it crashes expo-gl. Use CameraController with PanResponder.
- Camera always clamped inside room. No white space ever visible.
- Canvas background color must match ceiling material color.
- All camera values in useRef — never useState (prevents gesture re-render conflicts).
- Furniture floor plane rotation: [-Math.PI/2, -piece.rotation_y, 0], position [0, 0.002, 0]
- GLB models: useGLTF with Suspense wrapper at parent level

## Supabase Rules

- RLS enabled on all tables before any data is written
- Edge Functions runtime: Deno — never import Node.js modules
- Storage buckets: room-photos, renders, swipe-cards, assets (all private)
- Service role key only in Edge Function secrets — never in client code

## UI / Style

- Primary: #1B3A2D (dark forest green)
- Accent: #C47B3C (copper gold)
- Background: #F5F0E8 (warm cream)
- Never show style names (Japandi, Coastal, Bohemian, Mid-Century, Minimalist) in any user-facing UI except Profile where plain English aliases are used
- Font: System default (SF Pro on iOS)
- Never use white space behind the 3D room viewer
- Always use v0 first for screen UI. Never ask Cursor to design a screen's visual layout from scratch.

## AI / Render

- Render model: FLUX ControlNet Union Pro 2.0 via Replicate
- Depth estimation: Depth Anything V2 via Replicate
- AI assistant: Claude Sonnet 4 Vision via Anthropic API — through Edge Function only
- Product matching: OpenCLIP ViT-H-14 via Replicate — 1024-dim embeddings
- The app NEVER calls Replicate or Anthropic directly — always through Supabase Edge Functions

## Token Economy

- V1: tokens_enabled = false for all users. Balance shows 999, never decrements.
- Never gate any feature in V1 — token checks are infrastructure only.
  CURSORRULES
